upsc.append({"q":"Consider the following statements about the distribution of the hot, wet equatorial climate, per Goh Cheng Leong:\n1. It is found between about 5° and 10° north and south of the equator, with its greatest extent in the lowlands of the Amazon, the Zaire (Congo) basin, Malaysia and the East Indies.\n2. Further away from the equator, the influence of on-shore Trade Winds gives rise to a modified equatorial climate with monsoonal influences.\n3. Equatorial highlands, such as the Cameron Highlands in Malaysia and the Kenyan Highlands in East Africa, always experience the same hot temperatures as the equatorial lowlands, unmodified by altitude.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?","o":["1 and 2 only","1 and 3 only","2 and 3 only","1, 2 and 3"],"a":0,"e":"Statement 3 is incorrect — equatorial highlands are explicitly described as having a 'distinctively cooler climate, modified by altitude', not the same hot temperatures as the lowlands. Statements 1 and 2 are correct."})

