upsc.append({"q":"Match List-I (Region/Group) with List-II (Characteristic Forest Activity, per Goh Cheng Leong) and select the correct answer using the code below.\nList-I:\nA. Amazon basin Indian tribes\nB. Zaire basin Pygmies\nC. Malaysian Orang Asli\nList-II:\n1. Gather nuts\n2. Make cane products for sale to villages and towns\n3. Collect wild rubber\nCodes:","o":["A-3, B-1, C-2","A-1, B-3, C-2","A-3, B-2, C-1","A-2, B-1, C-3"],"a":0,"e":"The correct match is A-3, B-1, C-2: Amazon basin Indian tribes collect wild rubber; Zaire basin Pygmies gather nuts; and Malaysia's Orang Asli make cane products (from lianas/rattan) sold to villages and towns."})

upsc.append({"q":"Consider the following statements about plantation agriculture in the equatorial regions, per Goh Cheng Leong:\n1. Malaysia and Indonesia are the leading producers of natural rubber (Hevea brasiliensis), accounting for 44 and 24 per cent of world production respectively, though the plant originated in the Amazon basin as Para rubber.\n2. Brazil, the home country of rubber, remains among the world's top natural rubber exporters today.\n3. Ghana and the Ivory Coast are the two most important producers of cocoa, together accounting for the largest shares of world production, extensively cultivated in West Africa bordering the Gulf of Guinea.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?","o":["1 and 3 only","1 and 2 only","2 and 3 only","1, 2 and 3"],"a":0,"e":"Statement 2 is incorrect — the text explicitly states Brazil 'exports practically no natural rubber' today, despite being the plant's home country, due to tree diseases and lack of commercial organisation among Amazon lowland producers. Statements 1 and 3 are correct."})

