upsc.append({"q":"According to Koeppen's classification as presented by NCERT, which one of the following criteria defines Group A (Tropical) climates?","o":["The average temperature of the coldest month is 18°C or higher","Potential evaporation exceeds precipitation throughout the year","The average temperature of the coldest month is higher than minus 3°C but below 18°C","Average temperature for all months is below 10°C"],"a":0,"e":"Group A (Tropical) is defined by NCERT/Koeppen as having an average temperature of 18°C or higher in the coldest month. The other criteria describe Group B (Dry), Group C (Warm Temperate), and Group E (Cold) climates respectively, not Group A."})

upsc.append({"q":"Consider the following statements about the Tropical Wet (Af) climate type, according to NCERT — which directly corresponds to Goh Cheng Leong's 'Hot, Wet Equatorial Climate':\n1. It is found near the equator, with major areas in the Amazon Basin, western equatorial Africa, and the islands of the East Indies.\n2. Significant rainfall occurs in every month of the year, mostly as thunder showers in the afternoon, denoted by the small letter 'f' (no dry season).\n3. The annual range of temperature is considerable, as the maximum temperature on any day may be around 30°C while the minimum may fall below 5°C.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?","o":["1 and 2 only","1 and 3 only","2 and 3 only","1, 2 and 3"],"a":0,"e":"Statement 3 is incorrect — NCERT describes the annual range as negligible, with the maximum temperature on any day around 30°C and the minimum around 20°C (not falling below 5°C). Statements 1 and 2 are correct."})

upsc.append({"q":"Assertion (A): Tropical evergreen forests with dense canopy cover and large biodiversity are characteristic of the Af (Tropical Wet) climate.\nReason (R): The Af climate has uniformly high temperature and heavy, well-distributed rainfall throughout the year, providing continuously favourable conditions for luxuriant plant growth.\nWhich one of the following is correct in respect of the above Assertion (A) and Reason (R)?","o":["Both A and R are true, and R is the correct explanation of A","Both A and R are true, but R is NOT the correct explanation of A","A is true, but R is false","A is false, but R is true"],"a":0,"e":"Both are true and R correctly explains A — NCERT and Goh Cheng Leong both attribute the equatorial/Af climate's luxuriant, biodiverse evergreen forest cover precisely to its year-round high temperature and abundant, well-distributed rainfall, which never impose a dry or cold restriction on plant growth."})

